Lab: Referer-based access control 

Goal:-     This lab controls access to certain admin functionality based on the Referer header. You can familiarize yourself with the admin panel by logging in using the credentials administrator:admin.
To solve the lab, log in using the credentials wiener:peter and exploit the flawed access controls to promote yourself to become an administrator.

Observation:- #The application restricts access to admin functionality using the Referer header instead of proper authorization checks.
              #Admin actions include a Referer value pointing to /admin.
              #The server trusts the Referer header without verifying the user’s actual privileges.
              #A normal user can modify the request and manually set the Referer to /admin to perform admin level actions.

Steps to solve :- 
        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Login using administrator credential 
        Step3:- Change role of carlos from normal to administrator and capture the request in the burpsuit 
        step4:- now loging as given credential of normal user
        Step5:- go to my account and capture the reqest in burpsuit 
        Step6:- Change cookie session (replace carlos cookiee with wiener) change name from carlos to wiener while keeping refrer as /admin
        Step7:- Send reqest 

Root Cause:- #Access control decisions were based on a client controlled HTTP header (Referer).
             #The server assumed that requests originating from the admin page were legitimate without validating user roles.
             #Since headers can be easily modified, this resulted in access control bypass.

Vulnerability Type:- #Broken Access Control
                     #Referer based Access Control Bypass

